    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0513" n="421" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg421"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">President Wilson’s Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President to the Special Representative</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">House</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 30, 1918</hi>
                        </date><anchor n="1" xml:id="d348-f1"/>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Analysis of fourteen points<anchor n="2" xml:id="d348-f2"/> satisfactory
                    interpretation of principles involved but details of application mentioned
                    should be regarded as merely illustrative suggestions and reserved for peace
                    conference. Admission of inchoate nationalities to peace conference most
                    undesirable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d348-f1" n="1" xml:id="d348-f1-content">
                <p>Hour of dispatch not recorded.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d348-f2" n="2" xml:id="d348-f2-content">
                <p>Reference is to the Special Representative’s telegram No. 5 of Oct. 29, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg405">p. 405</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
